                    \-
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/3-algebra"} 3-algebra
                  %td{:style => "text-align: left;"}
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi Mod
                            %mi R
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Mod_R
                    \-
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/4-module"} 4-module
          %h2#related_concepts Related concepts
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vector+space"} vector space
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/module+category"}> module category
                , (“
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/actegory"}> actegory
                ”)
            %li
              %p
                %strong> 2-vector space
                ,
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-representation"} 2-representation
              %ul
                %li
                  %p
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-ring"} 2-ring
                %li
                  %p
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2Mod"} 2Mod
                %li
                  %p
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-vector+bundle"} 2-vector bundle
                %li
                  %p
                    %em
                      %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/TwoVect"} TwoVect
                    is a Mathematica software package for computer algebra with 2-vector spaces
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/n-vector+space"} n-vector space
          %h2#references References
          %h3#ReferencesAsnTuplesOfvectorSpaces
            As
            = succeed "-tuples" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
          %p
            The notion of 2-vector spaces as
            = succeed "-tuples" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
          %ul
            %li#KapranovVoevodsky91
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Mikhail+Kapranov"}> Mikhail Kapranov
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Vladimir+Voevodsky"} Vladimir Voevodsky
              %em
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mn 2
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 2
                \-categories and Zamolodchikov tetrahedra equations
              in
              = succeed "," do
                %em Algebraic groups and their generalization: quantum and infinite-dimensional methods
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a{:href => "https://www.math.ias.edu/vladimir/sites/math.ias.edu.vladimir/files/1994_Kapranov_Voevodsky.pdf"} pdf
          %h3#ReferencesAsTwoTermChainComplexes As 2-term chain complexes
          %p
            The notion of 2-vector spaces as 2-term
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/chain+complexes"} chain complexes
            is due to
          %ul
            %li#BaezCrans04
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/John+C.+Baez"}> John C. Baez
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Alissa+S.+Crans"} Alissa S. Crans
              = succeed "," do
                %em Higher-Dimensional Algebra VI: Lie 2-Algebras
              %strong 12
              (2004) 492-528 &amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/math/0307263"}> arXiv:math/0307263
              \&amp;rbrack;
          %p and used in
          %ul
            %li#Forrester-Barker
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Magnus+Forrester-Barker"}> Magnus Forrester-Barker
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em
                  Representations of Crossed Modules and
                  = succeed "-Groups" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %msup
                            %mi Cat
                            %mn 1
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Cat^1
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a{:href => "http://www.maths.bangor.ac.uk/research/ftp/theses/forrester-barker.pdf"} pdf
          %h3#ReferencesAsAlgebrasWithBimodules As algebras with bimodules between them
          %p
            The notion of 2-vector spaces with 2-linear maps between them as algebras with bimodules between them (subsuming the definition in
            %a{:href => "#KapranovVoevodsky91"} Kapranov &amp; Voevodsky 1991
            as the special case of algebras that are
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/direct+sums"} direct sums
            of the
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ground+field"} ground field
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Urs+Schreiber"}> Urs Schreiber
              , §A of:
              = succeed "," do
                %em AQFT from n-functorial QFT
              %strong 291
              (2009) 357-401 &amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/0806.1079"}> arXiv:0806.1079
              ,
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1007/s00220-009-0840-2"} doi:10.1007/s00220-009-0840-2
          %p following earlier discussion in
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Urs+Schreiber"}> Urs Schreiber
                ,
                %em
                  %a{:href => "https://golem.ph.utexas.edu/category/2006/10/topology_in_trondheim_and_kro.html"} 2-vectors in Trondheim
                (2006)
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Urs+Schreiber"}> Urs Schreiber
                ,
                %em
                  %a{:href => "https://golem.ph.utexas.edu/category/2007/11/2vectors_in_trondheim.html"} Topology in Trondheim and Kro, Baas &amp; Bökstedt on 2-vector bundles
                (2007)
          %p which is picked up in
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Urs+Schreiber"}> Urs Schreiber
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Konrad+Waldorf"} Konrad Waldorf
              = succeed "," do
                %em Connections on non-abelian Gerbes and their Holonomy
              %strong 28
              17 (2013) 476-540 &amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/0808.1923"}> arXiv:0808.1923
              ,
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a{:href => "http://www.tac.mta.ca/tac/volumes/28/17/28-17abs.html"} tac:28-17
          %p
            and further developed into a theory of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-vector+bundles"} 2-vector bundles
            (via algebra bundles with bundles of bimodules between them) in:
          %ul
            %li#KristelLudewigWaldorf22
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Peter+Kristel"}> Peter Kristel
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Matthias+Ludewig"} Matthias Ludewig
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Konrad+Waldorf"} Konrad Waldorf
              %em The insidious bicategory of algebra bundles
              \&amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2204.03900"}> arXiv:2204.03900
              \&amp;rbrack;
          %p Essentially the same notion also appears, apparently independently, in:
          %ul
            %li#FreedHopkinsTeleman09
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Daniel+S.+Freed"}> Daniel S. Freed
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Michael+J.+Hopkins"} Michael J. Hopkins
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jacob+Lurie"} Jacob Lurie
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Constantin+Teleman"} Constantin Teleman
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Topological+Quantum+Field+Theories+from+Compact+Lie+Groups"} Topological Quantum Field Theories from Compact Lie Groups
              \&amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/0905.0731"}> arXiv:0905.0731
              \&amp;rbrack;
          %p
            The notion is reviewed in a list of “standard” definitions in
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#BDSPV15"} BDSPV15
          %p See also at
          %ul
            %li
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometry+of+physics"}> geometry of physics
                \:
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometry+of+physics+-+modules"} geometry of physics - modules
          %p the section on 2-modules.
          %h3#further_discussion Further discussion
          %p Review includes
          %ul
            %li#BDSPV15
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Bruce+Bartlett"}> Bruce Bartlett
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Christopher+L.+Douglas"} Christopher L. Douglas
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Chris+Schommer-Pries"} Chris Schommer-Pries
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jamie+Vicary"} Jamie Vicary
              = succeed "," do
                %em A bestiary of 2–vector spaces
              %em Modular categories as representations of the 3-dimensional bordism 2-category
              \&amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1509.06811"}> arXiv:1509.06811
              \&amp;rbrack;
          %p
            Another definition of 2-modules over
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-rings"} 2-rings
            (see there for more) is in
          %ul
            %li#CJF
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Alexandru+Chirvasitu"}> Alexandru Chirvasitu
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Theo+Johnson-Freyd"} Theo Johnson-Freyd
              = succeed "," do
                %em The fundamental pro-groupoid of an affine 2-scheme
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "http://dx.doi.org/10.1007/s10485-011-9275-y"} DOI
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1105.3104"} arXiv:1105.3104
          %p
            A treatment of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-representations"} 2-representations
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+2-groups"} Lie 2-groups
            is in
          %ul
            %li
              Zhen Huan,
              %em 2-Representations of Lie 2-groups and 2-Vector Bundles
              (
              %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2208.10042"}> arXiv:2208.10042
              )
